1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:06,760
Often, the burden we carry inside becomes beyond our strength and sinks us into despair.

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,741
But we continue living.

3
00:00:09,501 --> 00:00:11,301
"I'm fine" is always our answer.

4
00:00:12,021 --> 00:00:16,101
But when we are alone with the Creator, there is something we murmur in whispers.

5
00:00:16,921 --> 00:00:17,881
How long, my Lord?

6
00:00:18,641 --> 00:00:19,561
When is my time?

7
00:00:20,221 --> 00:00:23,762
When will I too thank You, saying, "The Creator has done this for me"?

8
00:00:24,302 --> 00:00:24,702
When will it be?

9
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,382
Didn't You say, "Ask and it shall be given to you"?

10
00:00:27,922 --> 00:00:30,022
I am asking You, how long will You withhold it from me?

11
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:34,522
Being in darkness, it is hard to trust in God's working and timing.

12
00:00:35,182 --> 00:00:37,442
But the Creator is never late.

13
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:43,503
Just as at Cana He said "My hour has not yet come," the Creator knows everything you need.

14
00:00:44,463 --> 00:00:54,824
Not only what you asked, but far higher gifts than what you ask or imagine are in your God's hands; so wait in faith—you will not regret your waiting.

15
00:00:55,084 --> 00:00:59,544
Because those who rely on Him and wait will not be put to shame, nor have they ever been put to shame.

16
00:00:59,964 --> 00:01:04,044
The Gospel of John Chapter 2 tells us about the wedding that took place at Cana.

17
00:01:04,704 --> 00:01:17,865
The Gospel of John opens this scene with a few simple details: a wedding was taking place in Cana of Galilee; the mother of Jesus was there; Jesus and His disciples were also invited.

18
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:21,005
Then John tells us that the wine ran out.

19
00:01:21,425 --> 00:01:33,086
Though the story is short, its details are carefully set: the wedding, Mary's presence, Jesus and His disciples, and the shortage that was to be brought before Jesus.

20
00:01:33,786 --> 00:01:37,146
John does not tell us the names of the bridegroom and bride.

21
00:01:37,807 --> 00:01:42,227
Jesus is at the wedding, and in the middle of the joy, a shortage occurs.

22
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:44,387
This holds great meaning.

23
00:01:44,767 --> 00:01:48,067
Jesus is not distant from normal human life.

24
00:01:48,607 --> 00:01:51,067
He was invited to a wedding, and He came.

25
00:01:51,587 --> 00:01:54,568
The scene begins not with a sermon, but with His presence.

26
00:01:55,148 --> 00:01:58,168
John the Evangelist turns his focus to the Holy Virgin Mary.

27
00:01:58,728 --> 00:02:02,028
First of all, let us see how John describes Mary.

28
00:02:02,548 --> 00:02:09,509
"The mother of Jesus was there." The Gospel of John does not tell us where Mary sat or what she was doing.

29
00:02:09,949 --> 00:02:13,009
Nor does it explain how she realized the problem that arose.

30
00:02:13,409 --> 00:02:18,209
It only tells us that she was there and noticed the problem when it appeared.

31
00:02:18,609 --> 00:02:19,589
The wine had run out.

32
00:02:20,249 --> 00:02:23,270
We do not know if others knew about the problem.

33
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:28,310
What we know is that there was a problem and Mary noticed it.

34
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:35,670
Sometimes a celebration that looks full of joy from the outside can have a hidden problem within.

35
00:02:35,950 --> 00:02:42,171
Before the problem could embarrass the bridegroom and bride in front of people, Mary noticed what was missing.

36
00:02:42,731 --> 00:02:45,231
Some problems we can see from afar.

37
00:02:46,011 --> 00:02:50,351
But with some problems, people try hard to cover them up so others won't know.

38
00:02:50,811 --> 00:02:55,352
Even if someone is close to collapsing inside, they may continue their work.

39
00:02:55,932 --> 00:02:59,992
Another person, finding it hard to state the truth, may say "I'm doing fine."

40
00:03:00,612 --> 00:03:08,533
A family might show that everything is going well, yet inside carry a heavy burden they cannot share with others.

41
00:03:09,213 --> 00:03:13,473
But the Gospel does not ask us to assume we know everything about others' suffering.

42
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:20,813
Rather, Mary teaches us to view them with compassion, not forgetting that there may be a hidden struggle inside others.

43
00:03:20,813 --> 00:03:24,334
Mary saw that what was missing could ruin the joy of others.

44
00:03:24,334 --> 00:03:26,994
She did not spread the situation as gossip.

45
00:03:27,414 --> 00:03:29,434
Instead, she brought the problem to Jesus.

46
00:03:30,014 --> 00:03:34,834
"They have no wine," Mary said to Jesus; she did not start with a long explanation.

47
00:03:35,434 --> 00:03:37,875
She did not explain to Him how the problem came about.

48
00:03:38,335 --> 00:03:40,675
Nor did she give Him details of what might happen.

49
00:03:41,115 --> 00:03:42,655
She simply said this to Him:

50
00:03:43,155 --> 00:03:48,595
"They have no wine." These words were a request bringing the necessary need before her Son.

51
00:03:49,155 --> 00:03:52,295
Mary did not say, "You must do such and such."

52
00:03:52,896 --> 00:03:54,696
She only expressed what was missing.

53
00:03:55,436 --> 00:03:57,396
She placed the problem upon Jesus.

54
00:03:57,876 --> 00:04:00,336
When a problem comes, what do you do first?

55
00:04:00,956 --> 00:04:04,536
First of all, fall into panic, anxiety, despair?

56
00:04:05,196 --> 00:04:08,957
Or can we truly bring the problem as it is to Christ?

57
00:04:10,137 --> 00:04:13,517
The Gospel does not teach us that we can control God through prayer.

58
00:04:13,957 --> 00:04:17,817
Rather, it shows us that Mary brought a real problem to Jesus.

59
00:04:18,677 --> 00:04:24,198
And after that, we see the story continue according to Jesus' response and His divine mission.

60
00:04:24,898 --> 00:04:31,918
Therefore, without deciding in advance how God ought to answer us, we must learn to bring our problems to Christ.

61
00:04:32,458 --> 00:04:35,138
There is comfort seen in the words Mary spoke.

62
00:04:35,518 --> 00:04:40,579
Sometimes, overwhelmed by weakness, we do not have the strength to pray eloquently.

63
00:04:41,099 --> 00:04:42,999
We may not even know what to say.

64
00:04:43,339 --> 00:04:46,239
Sometimes we can only express what we are lacking.

65
00:04:46,739 --> 00:04:55,680
"Lord, I am afraid." "Lord, I don't know how to continue." "Lord, they have no wine." Prayer begins by telling Jesus the truth.

66
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:56,120
Then, Jesus answered her.

67
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,560
"My hour has not yet come"—this statement is not simple.

68
00:04:57,580 --> 00:05:00,000
Why did Jesus, who is able to supply what is lacking, answer like this when Mary presented the problem to Him?

69
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:14,561
Why, while the people who needed help were right before Him, did He choose to say His hour had not yet come?

70
00:05:15,361 --> 00:05:19,981
When John Chrysostom looks deeply into this statement, he clarifies an important point.

71
00:05:20,261 --> 00:05:22,021
Jesus is not ruled by time.

72
00:05:22,401 --> 00:05:25,122
He is the One who created time and set the order of time.

73
00:05:25,442 --> 00:05:31,442
Therefore, when He says "My hour has not yet come," it is not as a human waiting for time or bound by it.

74
00:05:31,842 --> 00:05:36,302
As John Chrysostom explains, God does not accomplish things without order.

75
00:05:36,822 --> 00:05:39,283
Every single thing is accomplished in its proper time.

76
00:05:39,903 --> 00:05:46,303
Creation, the coming of grace, the resurrection, and the coming judgment—all are not accomplished at once.

77
00:05:46,863 --> 00:05:49,583
John Chrysostom also explains another deeper reason.

78
00:05:50,383 --> 00:05:54,064
At that time, Jesus had not yet been fully revealed to many.

79
00:05:54,564 --> 00:05:58,044
Even His disciples had not yet fully understood His identity.

80
00:05:58,624 --> 00:06:06,864
Even the guests at the wedding, though they knew the wine ran out, did not yet understand who Jesus was and what He could do.

81
00:06:07,424 --> 00:06:08,865
So what was Jesus to do?

82
00:06:09,625 --> 00:06:15,345
Was He to give them what they needed by a miracle before people realized the shortage, before knowing what they needed?

83
00:06:15,785 --> 00:06:23,346
As John Chrysostom explains, when people truly realize their need, they understand and appreciate the help they receive even more.

84
00:06:23,686 --> 00:06:28,846
If a person does not realize their hunger, they do not fully understand how important the food given to them is.

85
00:06:29,246 --> 00:06:35,966
Likewise, if a person does not perceive their shortage, they cannot comprehend how great the help rendered to them is.

86
00:06:35,966 --> 00:06:38,427
Holy Virgin Mary did not argue.

87
00:06:38,427 --> 00:06:39,447
She did not compel her Son.

88
00:06:40,027 --> 00:06:45,227
When she heard that mystery-filled answer, she did what we often find hard to do.

89
00:06:45,787 --> 00:06:48,387
Mary did not tell them what to do.

90
00:06:48,387 --> 00:06:50,007
She did not tell them where to go.

91
00:06:50,487 --> 00:06:53,608
She did not explain what He would ask of them.

92
00:06:53,828 --> 00:06:56,808
She told them only one thing: "Whatever He tells you... do it."

93
00:06:57,388 --> 00:06:58,028
This is faith.

94
00:06:58,568 --> 00:07:01,828
Faith is not only when we have found answers to all our questions.

95
00:07:02,268 --> 00:07:07,468
Faith is believing that, even if we do not yet see the way, the Lord we believe in knows.

96
00:07:08,029 --> 00:07:12,449
It is when we stop trying to hold everything in our own hands and start leaning on His word.

97
00:07:13,029 --> 00:07:16,389
Perhaps we too are like the servants at the wedding.

98
00:07:17,029 --> 00:07:19,349
We do not know what the Lord might say to us.

99
00:07:19,849 --> 00:07:21,929
We do not know where His word will lead us.

100
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:25,910
Nor do we instantly understand what His command is for.

101
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:30,830
But what Mary teaches us is this: to obey before we understand everything.

102
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:33,070
To believe before we see everything.

103
00:07:33,610 --> 00:07:36,670
To trust that He hears us before everything is answered.

104
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:40,471
Between the problem and the answer, there was one statement.

105
00:07:40,911 --> 00:07:46,851
"Do whatever He tells you." Between our prayer and God's answer, there is a moment like that too.

106
00:07:47,231 --> 00:07:47,571
We pray.

107
00:07:48,091 --> 00:07:48,451
We wait.

108
00:07:48,891 --> 00:07:49,411
We ponder.

109
00:07:49,771 --> 00:07:50,971
And sometimes we grieve.

110
00:07:51,551 --> 00:08:02,052
"Lord, why?" "How long?" "When will the answer I requested come?" But perhaps in that silence, the Lord is showing us one small step ahead of us.

111
00:08:02,992 --> 00:08:07,813
Yet we might fail to see that small step while waiting for the grand answer to arrive.

112
00:08:08,653 --> 00:08:14,413
We want to see the opened door; but He may be indicating what we ought to do today.

113
00:08:15,473 --> 00:08:21,353
We want to know the coming outcome; but He may give us a word to obey today.

114
00:08:21,853 --> 00:08:26,474
Because faith does not ask us to know every outcome before we begin.

115
00:08:27,094 --> 00:08:29,994
It only asks us to trust in the Lord who walks with us.

116
00:08:30,734 --> 00:08:33,574
Perhaps this is what we too need to learn.

117
00:08:33,874 --> 00:08:35,554
To call upon Jesus in our trouble.

118
00:08:35,934 --> 00:08:37,715
To listen to His voice in our silence.

119
00:08:38,075 --> 00:08:39,755
To keep His word in our waiting.

120
00:08:40,275 --> 00:08:43,715
To believe that even in moments we do not understand, He knows.

121
00:08:44,155 --> 00:08:47,935
Because our hope is not in our full understanding (knowledge).

122
00:08:48,295 --> 00:08:49,695
It is in the Lord in whom we believe.

123
00:08:50,195 --> 00:08:53,736
At the wedding, the servants did not yet know what was about to happen.

124
00:08:54,316 --> 00:09:00,196
Perhaps in our lives too, the place where the greatest change begins is not when we have found all the answers.

125
00:09:00,776 --> 00:09:03,236
It is when we begin to listen to His word.

126
00:09:03,856 --> 00:09:07,917
As Jesus commanded them, the servants filled the water jars with water.

127
00:09:08,657 --> 00:09:09,117
Only water.

128
00:09:09,837 --> 00:09:11,797
What was visible to their eyes was just water.

129
00:09:12,657 --> 00:09:14,517
What was in their mind was also just water.

130
00:09:15,137 --> 00:09:17,817
But they did not know what the Lord was going to do.

131
00:09:18,437 --> 00:09:22,357
And Jesus said to them, "Now draw some out and take it to the master of the feast."

132
00:09:22,838 --> 00:09:24,098
And the servants took it to him.

133
00:09:24,578 --> 00:09:26,518
When the master of the feast tasted the wine, he was amazed.

134
00:09:26,878 --> 00:09:28,338
What he tasted was indeed wine.

135
00:09:28,798 --> 00:09:30,698
It was not the wine served at the beginning.

136
00:09:31,058 --> 00:09:35,058
To the master's joy, the wine that came was fine wine, better than the first.

137
00:09:35,838 --> 00:09:37,539
This was not done by human power.

138
00:09:38,059 --> 00:09:40,239
Jesus turned the water into wine.

139
00:09:40,719 --> 00:09:44,599
What in human eyes was water was transformed into wine by the word of Jesus.

140
00:09:45,119 --> 00:09:49,719
At this time, Jesus revealed His glory, and His disciples believed in Him.

141
00:09:50,379 --> 00:09:53,640
The servants did not know what Jesus was going to do.

142
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:57,140
Nor did the master of the feast know where the wine came from.

143
00:09:57,660 --> 00:10:00,000
And all who were at the wedding might not have understood what had taken place.

144
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:03,740
But Jesus knew.

145
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:07,341
We too pass through times like that in our lives.

146
00:10:07,801 --> 00:10:09,421
The answer we are waiting for has not come.

147
00:10:09,861 --> 00:10:11,541
What we asked for has not been fulfilled.

148
00:10:12,041 --> 00:10:14,661
And the path ahead of us seems dark.

149
00:10:15,481 --> 00:10:16,921
In that time, what do we think?

150
00:10:17,421 --> 00:10:24,862
"Lord, where are You?" "What are You doing?" "How long shall I wait?" Perhaps these questions are in our hearts.

151
00:10:25,362 --> 00:10:27,062
The servants filled the water.

152
00:10:27,882 --> 00:10:29,582
But Jesus performed the miracle.

153
00:10:30,162 --> 00:10:36,463
We too can fulfill the responsibility before us, walk in faith, and do what is right.

154
00:10:37,023 --> 00:10:38,603
But the outcome is in God's hand.

155
00:10:39,423 --> 00:10:43,303
This does not mean all our problems will be solved quickly as we desire.

156
00:10:43,963 --> 00:10:50,404
But what the story of Cana teaches us is to know who Jesus is, to listen to His word, and to believe in Him.

157
00:10:50,924 --> 00:10:52,204
At Cana, the wine ran out.

158
00:10:52,764 --> 00:10:54,284
But Jesus was there.

159
00:10:54,784 --> 00:10:57,284
This is the thought we ought to keep in our hearts.

160
00:10:57,964 --> 00:11:00,404
In our lives too, there are times when joy seems lacking.

161
00:11:01,065 --> 00:11:08,325
Times when our hope weakens, when our prayers seem unanswered, when we carry inside a pain we do not wish to tell others.

162
00:11:08,885 --> 00:11:14,286
At that time, we need to remember not only to look at our problem, but also that the Lord is with us.

163
00:11:14,846 --> 00:11:16,246
So what do we learn today?

164
00:11:16,606 --> 00:11:19,086
From Mary we learn this: let us draw near to Jesus.

165
00:11:19,626 --> 00:11:23,846
From the servants we learn this: let us hear His word, let us do what He commands us.

166
00:11:24,306 --> 00:11:28,847
From the miracle we learn this: what we cannot do, Jesus can do.

167
00:11:29,347 --> 00:11:31,767
Perhaps in your life right now, the wine has run out.

168
00:11:32,147 --> 00:11:33,387
Perhaps the answer has not come.

169
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:35,467
Perhaps the path has not opened.

170
00:11:36,047 --> 00:11:39,767
Mary said to the servants, "Do whatever He tells you."

171
00:11:40,227 --> 00:11:41,948
That word is for us today as well.

172
00:11:42,128 --> 00:11:43,988
Are we ready to hear what the Lord says to us?

173
00:11:44,408 --> 00:11:46,828
Are we ready to follow the path He leads us on?

174
00:11:47,508 --> 00:11:51,328
Are we ready to trust in Him even when we do not understand?

175
00:11:51,808 --> 00:11:53,388
May God grant peace to your hearts.

176
00:11:53,988 --> 00:11:56,269
May He strengthen your faith during your time of waiting.

177
00:11:56,789 --> 00:11:59,409
May He give you His grace to hear and follow His word.
